---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import {
  ToastCustomList,
  ToastIsolated,
  ToastPlayground,
  ToastPromise,
  ToastWithAction,
} from '../../components/ToastDemo';
---

<Docs title="Toast" description="Short notices that stack in a corner and dismiss themselves.">
  <h1 class="docs-title">Toast</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A short notice about something that just happened: a save, a failed upload, a sent invite. Toasts stack in the
    bottom corner, close on their own, and never take focus away from what someone is doing.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8" id="toast-demo">
    <ToastPlayground client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Toast usage"
      code={`import { Toaster, toast } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/toast";

// Once, near the root of the app.
<Toaster>
  <App />
</Toaster>

// Anywhere, inside or outside React.
toast.add({
  title: "Invite sent",
  description: "Ana Ruiz can now join the Meadow workspace.",
  type: "success",
});`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>Toaster</code> mounts a provider and a ready-made viewport. Call <code>toast.add</code> from event handlers,
      data hooks, or plain modules; it returns an id you can pass to <code>toast.update</code> or{' '}
      <code>toast.close</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Types</h2>
    <p>
      <code>type</code> picks the icon: <code>"success"</code> (check), <code>"error"</code> (a cross in the danger
      color), <code>"warning"</code> (triangle), <code>"info"</code> (circle), and <code>"loading"</code> (spinner).
      Leave it out for a plain toast with no icon. Toasts close after 5 seconds unless you pass another{' '}
      <code>timeout</code>; <code>{'timeout: 0'}</code> keeps one open until it’s dismissed.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Actions</h2>
    <p>
      Pass <code>actionProps</code> to add one small outline button. Its <code>children</code> are the label and its{' '}
      <code>onClick</code> runs before the toast closes. Keep the action optional: the same result must be reachable
      elsewhere, because the toast can close before someone reaches it.
    </p>
    <ToastWithAction client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Isolated managers</h2>
    <p>
      <code>createToastManager()</code> makes a separate stack. Hand it to{' '}
      <code>{'<Toaster toastManager={manager}>'}</code> and call <code>useToastManager().add</code> from components
      inside it. Create it once, for example with <code>useState(createToastManager)</code>.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Isolated manager"
      code={`function Controls() {
  const manager = useToastManager();
  return (
    <Button onClick={() => manager.add({ title: "Success example", type: "success", timeout: 5000 })}>
      success
    </Button>
  );
}

export function Example() {
  const [manager] = useState(createToastManager);
  return (
    <Toaster toastManager={manager}>
      <Controls />
    </Toaster>
  );
}`}
    />
    <ToastIsolated client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Loading and results</h2>
    <p>
      <code>toast.promise</code> shows a <code>"loading"</code> toast while the promise runs, then replaces it in place
      with the <code>success</code> or <code>error</code> options. Each option can be a function of the result or the
      error.
    </p>
    <ToastPromise client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Custom layout</h2>
    <p>
      For a different layout, compose the parts yourself: <code>ToastProvider</code>, <code>ToastPortal</code>{' '}
      (optional), <code>ToastViewport</code>, and a list of <code>Toast</code> roots read from{' '}
      <code>useToastManager().toasts</code>, each holding <code>ToastContent</code>, <code>ToastTitle</code>,{' '}
      <code>ToastDescription</code>, <code>ToastAction</code>, and <code>ToastClose</code>. Title and description fill
      themselves from the toast; the action renders only when it has a label.
    </p>
    <ToastCustomList client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="toast-api">
    <h2 class="section-title">API</h2>
    <p>
      <code>Toaster</code> takes every <code>ToastProvider</code> prop: <code>toastManager</code> (defaults to the
      shared <code>toast</code>), <code>timeout</code> (5000), and <code>limit</code> (3 visible).{' '}
      <code>toast.add</code> takes <code>title</code>, <code>description</code>, <code>type</code>, <code>timeout</code>
      , <code>priority</code>, <code>actionProps</code>, <code>onClose</code>, and <code>data</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>ToastAction</code> renders a small outline <code>Button</code> and <code>ToastClose</code> a small ghost
      icon button labeled “Close toast”; pass <code>render</code> to swap either. <code>Toast</code> takes{' '}
      <code>swipeDirection</code>
      (down and right by default). Every part sets a <code>data-slot</code>, and <code>toastTypeNames</code> lists the
      types with icons.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The viewport is a polite live region named “Notifications”, so new toasts are announced without moving focus.
      Press F6 to jump to the stack; Tab then moves through each toast’s action and close button, and focus returns
      where it was when the stack empties. Hovering or focusing the stack expands it and pauses every timer. Swipe a
      toast away on touch screens. Pass <code>{'priority: "high"'}</code> for an urgent error that should be announced
      right away.
    </p>
    <p>
      Toasts slide up over 180ms and the stack reflows over 120–180ms. With reduced motion they only fade. In
      forced-colors mode each toast keeps a visible border.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Toasts use <code>--sprout-surface</code>, <code>--sprout-line</code>, <code>--sprout-text</code>,{' '}
      <code>--sprout-muted</code>, <code>--sprout-danger</code> for the error icon,
      <code>--sprout-shadow-overlay</code>, and the panel radius. They need no brand color, so they look the same with
      the neutral and TulipFarm themes in light and dark mode.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
